WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:54.840
<b>Gear Second</b>

3
00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:58.640
Gear? Your techniques have changed?

4
00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:03.850
Are you supposed to be a steam engine? You
certainly are full of hot air.

5
00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.520
You're starting to test my patience.

6
00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.200
The truth is I'm glad I met you guys when I
did.

7
00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.120
Gum-Gum...

8
00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:25.250
What, are you stopping to aim? That only gives
me more time to dodge.

9
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.960
Fine. Let's see how good your aim is, then.

10
00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:30.420
Shave!

11
00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.420
Jet Pistol!

12
00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:44.980
Rifle!

13
00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.860
I can't see him at all!

14
00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.210
Stamp!

15
00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.740
And spear!

16
00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.210
Missile!

17
00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.510
Impossible.

18
00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.400
No, it has to be.

19
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.440
The truth is I'm glad
I met you guys when I did.

20
00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.340
He's using the Shave technique.

21
00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:38.300
Only CP9 should know the Six Powers,
but he's clearly mastered it.

22
00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:41.910
Air Door!

23
00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.880
Huh?

24
00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.280
He disappeared.

25
00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:50.500
This is unheard of.

26
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.270
A pirate commanding
one of our techniques?

27
00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:55.990
This is a sick joke.

28
00:03:55.990 --> 00:04:00.230
Don't tell me he was
capable of this all along!

29
00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:04.200
No, it doesn't matter.

30
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.930
No one can match the speed
of a true Six Powers master!

31
00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.340
I won't lose to him!

32
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.910
If I turn his body parts
into doors like before,

33
00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:17.180
that should stop him
dead in his tracks.

34
00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:22.290
After that, all I have
to do is finish him off.

35
00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:23.730
Door-Door!

36
00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:32.380
When we fought before, and it looked like you
were disappearing,

37
00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:36.880
you were really just moving your feet ten or
twenty times a second.

38
00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.010
I got the hang of it, too.

39
00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:42.180
But I never would've figured something like
that out on my own.

40
00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.930
Gum-Gum...

41
00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.850
I can take it. I'll use my strongest defense!

42
00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.860
Iron Body. Strength!

43
00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.110
Jet Bazooka!

44
00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.730
You sure are tough, aren't you?

45
00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:16.340
All right then.

46
00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:19.310
I was gonna save it, but
I have an even better trick.

47
00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:20.970
Don't blink.

48
00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.640
I call this...

49
00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.070
Man, I'm beat.

50
00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:42.180
Guess my body can't
keep this up for long.

51
00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.380
Well, I don't care
about my body right now.

52
00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.850
I need to move ahead.

53
00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:55.790
<b>Courthouse</b>

54
00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.250
<b>Gates of Justice</b>

55
00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:56.870
<b>Tower of Justice</b>

56
00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:57.960
<b>Island Gate</b>

57
00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.960
<b>Courthouse</b>

58
00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.930
Damn it! What's going on here?

59
00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:02.530
Quick! Fire the cannons, men!

60
00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.000
Before they step on us!

61
00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:06.620
Yeah, nice try!

62
00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.940
But those peashooters
aren't enough to stop me!

63
00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:13.240
You can run or you can fight, little men,
but we're comin' through either way!

64
00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.330
I see it and I still can't believe it!

65
00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:22.580
I don't know what you said to those guys,
but it must've been something else!

66
00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:24.810
We warriors understand each other!

67
00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.150
The time has come, brothers!

68
00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.820
The courthouse is
looming on the horizon.

69
00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.180
Onward!

70
00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:34.160
<b>Island Gate</b>
<b>Tower of Justice</b>

71
00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.160
<b>Courthouse</b>

72
00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.140
What're you doing?

73
00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:36.420
Hurry up and go inside already!

74
00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:38.460
The pirates are in the
courthouse, aren't they?

75
00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.330
Yeah, but the problem
is there's a big frog

76
00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.430
at the door and he's
not letting anyone in!

77
00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:44.740
A frog?

78
00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.100
Keep fighting, Yokozuna!

79
00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:50.000
Don't give 'em an inch!

80
00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.340
We can't stop until the
drawbridge comes down!

81
00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:56.280
If those guys break our line of defense,
thousands of 'em could pour in here!

82
00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.080
Gero!

83
00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.530
<b>Courthouse Right Tower</b>

84
00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:05.010
Only one of us needs to get through!

85
00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:09.340
Even if everyone else falls, as long
as someone pulls that lever, we've won!

86
00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.870
<b>Courthouse Left Tower</b>

87
00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:20.690
You okay, Sis?

88
00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:23.400
Don't worry about me!

89
00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.240
All that matters is
bringing down that bridge

90
00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:28.140
and making sure the Straw Hats
get to the Tower of Law!

91
00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:28.840
Hold it!

92
00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.140
You're not going anywhere!

93
00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:31.140
Oh yeah?

94
00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.380
Try and stop me!

95
00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:39.140
What are those pirates plotting?

96
00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:43.330
Why's it so important
for them to go upstairs, huh?

97
00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:47.480
You won't get an answer outta me!

98
00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:48.880
We'll see about that!

99
00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.850
But I'll tell you one thing... you're
gonna pay if you hurt our big bro!

100
00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:55.450
<b>Courthouse Courtroom</b>

101
00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:56.630
After them!

102
00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:58.890
Bring those pirates down!

103
00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:02.760
How many of these stupid guards are we
gonna have to beat before they catch a hint?

104
00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:05.430
There they are!

105
00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:06.430
Attack!

106
00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:08.260
Move!

107
00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:12.370
Hey, if you have to throw them,
at least don't throw them at me!

108
00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.800
Guilty! Guilty!

109
00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.110
Guilty! Guilty! Guilty!

110
00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:18.270
Guilty! Guilty!

111
00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:19.310
Guilty! Guilty! Guilty!

112
00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:20.280
Would you guys shut up?

113
00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:21.940
I'm trying to think here.

114
00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.150
Must've taken a wrong turn somewhere.

115
00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.400
<b>Tower of Justice</b>

116
00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.530
You want us to take
Franky and Nico Robin

117
00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:37.140
to the Gates of Justice now?

118
00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:37.840
Yes!

119
00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:38.540
Do it!

120
00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:39.400
Quickly!

121
00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:40.640
But we're way ahead of schedule.

122
00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:42.570
The escort ship isn't even ready yet.

123
00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:43.740
I don't care!

124
00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:46.580
We can just wait for it on
the other side of the gates!

125
00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.610
If we get rid of those two,

126
00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.150
There's no point in
risking another battle

127
00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:55.320
with those monsters when we have
the power to end this right now!

128
00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:59.290
And while you're at it, gather
all the members of CP9, too!

129
00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:00.390
Sir!

130
00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:05.300
Now.

131
00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:09.830
It seems as if your one-way trip to hell
will be departing ahead of schedule.

132
00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:14.610
Then, we'll have all the time in
the world to deal with your friends!

133
00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:22.050
Those pirates sure know how to
bring the party, don't they?

134
00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:25.880
I don't know if they have common sense,
but they sure as heck have guts!

135
00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:27.820
Just you wait and watch, Chimney.

136
00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:31.290
In the end, whether they live
or die, that Straw Hat boy

137
00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:35.760
and all of his little friends are gonna
shake things up the whole world over.

138
00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:39.280
In hundreds of years, nobody's
pulled a stunt like this one!

139
00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:41.290
Mark my words.

140
00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:44.990
When this battle is over, every
man, woman, and child

141
00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:48.690
is gonna know the
name of Straw Hat Luffy!

142
00:09:55.140 --> 00:10:00.210
Robin!

143
00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.830
Yeah! He made it!

144
00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:05.300
Luffy!

145
00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:09.800
I'm here to save you!

146
00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:14.270
Chief Spandam, sir, there's a man in a straw
hat standing on the courthouse rooftop

147
00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.090
who's shouting things at Nico Robin!

148
00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:19.800
I wasn't able to confirm his identity
up close, but I assume it must be Luffy!

149
00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:20.780
On the rooftop?

150
00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:24.250
How could that happen when I saw
Blueno up there just a second ago?

151
00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:27.810
I thought he was
keeping watch! That idiot!

152
00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:30.180
What the hell is he doing?

153
00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:38.830
Guess I've been running
around a lot, huh?

154
00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.300
Man, time for a snack!

155
00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.770
Good thing I came prepared!

156
00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:48.260
Meat time!

157
00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:54.220
I knew putting these in my
pockets was a good idea!

158
00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:57.660
I just wish I had more pockets!

159
00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:04.220
So that's him, huh?

160
00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:05.890
Straw Hat Luffy.

161
00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.330
But what the hell is going on here?

162
00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:11.230
If Blueno was up there,
he should have...

163
00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:15.600
It can't be.

164
00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:17.800
No, he couldn't have...

165
00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.400
Blueno's a member of CP-9!

166
00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.940
A Six Powers master!

167
00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:23.870
With Devil Fruit powers, no less!

168
00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.340
His power level is superhuman!

169
00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:29.640
All right! Ready for round 2!

170
00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:34.250
How could that scrawny
brat ever defeat him?

171
00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.370
Ch-chief Spandam, sir,
how should we proceed?

172
00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:45.310
Lucci! Where is he?

173
00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:47.980
Somebody call him, now!

174
00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:49.810
And the rest of CP9, too!

175
00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:50.880
I've had enough.

176
00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:53.150
I won't be satisfied until
they wipe out Straw Hat

177
00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:55.400
and everyone in his wretched crew!

178
00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.200
And while you're at it,
tell Baskerville that

179
00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.040
if he lets the Straw Hats
lower that bridge,

180
00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:02.440
I'm going to send all
three of his heads rolling!

181
00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:04.170
Yes sir!

182
00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:08.450
Hey.

183
00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.810
Get that chin up, Nico Robin.

184
00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:15.870
You know, most people wouldn't
come here to save their friends.

185
00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.970
Hell, most people couldn't
even make it here at all.

186
00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:22.240
Don't get me wrong, I know
the only reason you agreed

187
00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:26.550
to the Government's terms was so you could
protect 'em, but you saw what happened.

188
00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:30.580
They don't give a damn about keeping
their word to you or anyone else.

189
00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.460
The deal is shot.

190
00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:35.660
Even if you keep your end of the bargain,
it's not gonna help anyone.

191
00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:39.630
Only thing left is to wait for your
crew to break you outta this dump.

192
00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:41.960
Doesn't sound so bad to me.

193
00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:46.370
And yet, here you are,
looking as miserable as ever.

194
00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:50.170
I get the feeling you're running from
something even your friends don't know about.

195
00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:56.410
I wouldn't worry about the
Straw Hats dying in this place,

196
00:12:56.410 --> 00:13:00.550
but if you can't look 'em in the eye,
in the end, they won't be able to save you.

197
00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:04.180
Hey! Is anybody there?

198
00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:11.690
Well, whether you like it or not,
I'm gonna make you face him.

199
00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:12.600
Huh?

200
00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.210
Listen up, all of you!

201
00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:19.550
We're putting Nico Robin out of
Straw Hat's reach immediately!

202
00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:21.450
Come with me to the Gates of Justice.

203
00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:22.920
Bring the prisoners!

204
00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:24.580
Bu...but Chief!

205
00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:26.920
No buts, just do it!

206
00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:27.750
Well... uh.

207
00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:30.790
There's one giant butt
that's a big problem!

208
00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:32.490
Ah!

209
00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:35.150
What the hell is that?

210
00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:36.810
Oh, hey Spanda.

211
00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:39.050
Like you said, I'm pretty much screwed,

212
00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:41.580
so I figured I might as
well blow myself up, y'know.

213
00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:42.590
What?

214
00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:46.220
That way, at least I get to take
your sorry ass with me when I go.

215
00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.790
You fool! Wait a minute, will you?

216
00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:52.750
When my butt goes off, the explosion's
gonna be at least a mile wide.

217
00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:56.560
Not much point in running,
but you might as well try.

218
00:13:56.560 --> 00:14:00.270
I don't know what's going on in
your pants, but please make it stop!

219
00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:05.670
Three... two... Damn it,
I can't die at a time like this!

220
00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:07.280
One!

221
00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:10.350
Stop it!

222
00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:13.030
Time to go, Robin!

223
00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:18.600
Coup de Boo!

224
00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:24.580
Good!

225
00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:26.310
The chains are broken, too!

226
00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:29.350
We're falling!

227
00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:33.090
Super!

228
00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:46.120
That was a close one.

229
00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:50.350
Good thing that fence was
there to catch us, huh?

230
00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:52.190
Hey.

231
00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:54.260
You didn't get hurt, did you?

232
00:14:58.330 --> 00:14:59.730
If I had another bottle of cola,

233
00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:03.330
I could get us to the other
side with a Coup de Vent.

234
00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.240
Hey, check it out.

235
00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:06.840
Straw Hat's over there.

236
00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:10.480
Now's your chance,
better give him your answer.

237
00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:11.480
He tricked us!

238
00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:12.350
Chief!

239
00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:16.450
Franky and Nico Robin broke the
chains and went out on the balcony!

240
00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:18.220
Then what are you waiting for, stupid?

241
00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:19.460
Capture them already!

242
00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:22.290
If you let them get away, I'll
send you all to the gallows!

243
00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:24.100
What?

244
00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:33.870
Hey, Robin!

245
00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:35.300
You're still there!

246
00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.230
Didn't you hear me yelling?

247
00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:39.460
Luffy.

248
00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:40.630
Don't let them get away!

249
00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:42.090
Grab them before they run!

250
00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:44.360
I don't have time
for you thugs right now!

251
00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.300
Weapons Left!

252
00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.440
Guess that mean's Franky's there, too.

253
00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:54.140
'Kay! I'll be right over!

254
00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:57.680
It's a little far, but I can make it!

255
00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:05.740
Gum-Gum...

256
00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:07.940
Stop it!

257
00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:16.130
How many times do I have to tell you?

258
00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:17.230
I'm not coming back!

259
00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:19.300
I'm not part of your crew anymore!

260
00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:20.980
Just go away!

261
00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:22.890
I don't want to see
your face ever again!

262
00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:23.950
Don't you understand?

263
00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.470
Why did you come to
save me in the first place?

264
00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:29.070
Why can't you just let me go?

265
00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:31.720
I never asked for this!

266
00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:33.790
You've gone too far!

267
00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.550
For the last time.

268
00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:37.790
I don't want you here!

269
00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:49.200
Do you hear me? I just want to die!

270
00:16:53.410 --> 00:16:57.310
Now this is
entertainment! What a twist!

271
00:16:58.740 --> 00:16:59.980
What the hell are you trying to pull?

272
00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:03.680
Your friends put their lives on
the line to come here, and you...

273
00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:05.730
They decided to do that on their own.

274
00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:06.700
Are you kidding me?

275
00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.800
Who cares if...

276
00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:14.350
You're in the way.

277
00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:17.560
What's wrong, Kaku?

278
00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:19.120
Venting your anger?

279
00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:21.760
'Cause your Devil Fruit
powers are so lame?

280
00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:22.790
Oh, shut up already!

281
00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:25.530
I like my powers just fine!

282
00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:29.500
Oh?

283
00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:32.200
All this ruckus for one little pirate?

284
00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:33.370
Yoyoi!

285
00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:39.440
Alone though he may be,
his perseverance is certainly admirable!

286
00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:43.650
I'll be damned.

287
00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:47.620
So he beat Blueno
after all! What a fool!

288
00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:52.290
Being a barkeep for five years probably
didn't do his fighting skills any favors.

289
00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:55.130
So it would appear,
but it's still a surprise.

290
00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:58.670
Either way, he lost! Chapapa!

291
00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:03.580
I'm glad you could all make it, CP9!

292
00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:05.550
And just in time, too!

293
00:18:05.550 --> 00:18:08.380
It seems the Straw Hats
are having a little tiff!

294
00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:10.820
It's quite amusing!

295
00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:13.650
You really shouldn't miss it!

296
00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:27.230
Good work out there,
Yokozuna! Keep it up!

297
00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:28.630
Gero!

298
00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:38.340
Guilty.

299
00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:40.110
Yes!

300
00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:41.610
It's the Guilty Jury!

301
00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:42.580
Step aside.

302
00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.310
It's time for that frog
to hear its verdict.

303
00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:49.090
Gero?

304
00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:56.990
Guilty!

305
00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:14.220
Ugh! Just what we need, more weirdos!

306
00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:16.910
Guilty! Guilty!

307
00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:20.380
Let's get 'em, Chopper...wait,
I mean, go get 'em, Chopper!

308
00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:22.950
What? Me? Alone?

309
00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:24.180
I gotta admit.

310
00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:27.850
I never thought there'd be an
actual judge on this island.

311
00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:33.750
I heard that the people who get taken
here are already considered guilty,

312
00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:38.540
so the Marines just lead the poor saps
through an empty court without even stopping.

313
00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:40.810
I'm afraid you're mistaken, pirate.

314
00:19:40.810 --> 00:19:43.510
On the contrary, this
courthouse carries the integrity

315
00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:45.710
of the greatest authority in the world.

316
00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:48.680
Even scum like you are
given a trial by jury.

317
00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:49.650
However.

318
00:19:49.650 --> 00:19:53.020
The jury here consists
entirely of former pirates

319
00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:56.000
who have been condemned to death
row in this very courtroom.

320
00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:59.670
Therefore, their only desire is
to drag others down with them.

321
00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:04.020
Tattoo: "Guilty"

322
00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:06.850
This place really is the gate
to the underworld, isn't it?

323
00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:09.550
Thus, in all the trials
carried out on this island.

324
00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:10.560
Not once.

325
00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:14.600
Has any criminal
been found 'not guilty'!

326
00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:15.300
Kiwi!

327
00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:16.410
Oh no!

328
00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.740
Guilty!

329
00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:25.940
Guilty!

330
00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:27.670
Damn, they're too strong!

331
00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:29.980
We can't give up now!

332
00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:33.020
If we don't bring down that
drawbridge, it's all over!

333
00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:35.960
Remember, Straw Hat is the one
who's gonna rescue our Bro.

334
00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.190
If we can't help him with this,

335
00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:40.460
then we have no right to call
ourselves the Franky Family!

336
00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.500
Gero!

337
00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:46.370
Yokozuna!

338
00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:51.410
You took all of those blows for
us and never budged an inch!

339
00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:54.520
I'll avenge you!

340
00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:58.430
Don't bother! We've
still got 6,000 marines!

341
00:20:58.430 --> 00:20:59.130
Now!

342
00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:01.070
Let's storm the courthouse, men!

343
00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:03.570
Crush those pirates!

344
00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:10.810
Gero.

345
00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:20.760
What's going on?

346
00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:22.570
Why are the giants here?

347
00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:26.670
It's the frog!

348
00:21:26.670 --> 00:21:28.500
What's the situation here?

349
00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:30.940
Wait. I know you!

350
00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:32.610
You're with the Straw Hats!

351
00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:34.780
What are you doing with those giants?

352
00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:38.780
Can't believe he held off all
those marines on his own!

353
00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:42.590
Yeah, he's one hell of a frog!

354
00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:53.400
Where did they run off to?

355
00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:55.590
They must've gotten lost again.

356
00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:58.330
We don't have time for this crap.

357
00:21:59.560 --> 00:22:04.140
Oh yeah, as long as I go up,
everything should work out fine.

358
00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:06.310
Tatsu maki!

359
00:22:11.860 --> 00:22:14.400
Huh? What?

360
00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:18.660
We better keep moving!

361
00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:33.410
You pirates really are in a
league of your own, aren't you?

362
00:22:33.860 --> 00:22:36.310
You're even strong enough
to order giants around!

363
00:22:36.310 --> 00:22:38.040
It's almost scary, really.

364
00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:42.410
Hm? Well... uh... 
Oh, by the way, your other crewmates

365
00:22:42.410 --> 00:22:44.280
are headed to the roof right now.

366
00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:45.120
The roof?

367
00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:46.810
You should go meet them!

368
00:22:46.810 --> 00:22:48.180
Leave that one to me.

369
00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:50.510
I'll get you there in a flash.

370
00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:51.780
Huh?

371
00:22:56.940 --> 00:22:59.040
You wanna die?

372
00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:00.610
That's right.

373
00:23:04.710 --> 00:23:05.970
Wait a second, Chief.

374
00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:07.600
Why are we listening to this crap

375
00:23:07.600 --> 00:23:10.140
when we could just go over
and pound that guy's face in?

376
00:23:10.140 --> 00:23:12.210
Patience, patience!

377
00:23:12.210 --> 00:23:13.280
Here we have a captain

378
00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:15.580
who risked his life to
save one of his crewmates

379
00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:19.380
only to have his precious hopes
dashed at the very last second.

380
00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:21.350
How tragic!

381
00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:23.290
And yet I can't tear my eyes away!

382
00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:24.760
It's too amusing!

383
00:23:24.760 --> 00:23:25.970
Robin!

384
00:23:25.970 --> 00:23:29.570
I don't know what to say.

385
00:23:30.370 --> 00:23:32.010
Wow, could he be more pathetic?

386
00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:34.540
I gotta see the look on his face!

387
00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:38.510
Sorry, but that sounds dumb to me.

388
00:23:40.380 --> 00:23:42.720
He's picking his nose?

389
00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:46.350
Listen, that won't work.

390
00:23:46.350 --> 00:23:48.920
We're already here,
and it was a lot of trouble.

391
00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:02.030
So we're gonna go ahead and save you.

392
00:24:02.030 --> 00:24:03.830
Landed.

393
00:24:05.720 --> 00:24:08.430
And if you still wanna die
after we're all back together.

394
00:24:09.710 --> 00:24:13.310
Well, that's your choice.

395
00:24:15.500 --> 00:24:17.100
Ow, ow ow.

396
00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:19.470
Looks like you landed on
your head...are you okay?

397
00:24:19.470 --> 00:24:20.840
Yeah, I'll be fine.

398
00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:24.000
What the heck happened back there?

399
00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:27.130
I think I might have
an idea of who to blame.

400
00:24:36.160 --> 00:24:37.000
There we go.

401
00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:39.730
That was a lot easier than
dealing with those stupid stairs.

402
00:24:39.730 --> 00:24:40.770
There he is!

403
00:24:40.770 --> 00:24:42.030
I knew it was you!

404
00:24:42.030 --> 00:24:43.870
You're lucky we got
out of the way in time!

405
00:24:43.870 --> 00:24:46.310
If that thing had hit us
head-on, we'd be dead right now!

406
00:24:46.310 --> 00:24:48.870
Oh, you're here, too?

407
00:24:51.050 --> 00:24:53.030
Dash!

408
00:24:53.030 --> 00:24:55.100
Boar Stew Shoot!

409
00:24:57.190 --> 00:24:59.110
I'm the first one here, no doubt.

410
00:24:59.110 --> 00:25:01.040
I've left Robin waiting long enough.

411
00:25:01.040 --> 00:25:04.080
Time for her prince to...Moss head?

412
00:25:04.380 --> 00:25:05.350
What are you doing here?

413
00:25:05.350 --> 00:25:06.950
You're gonna ruin everything!

414
00:25:06.950 --> 00:25:08.680
Finally made it, huh?

415
00:25:08.680 --> 00:25:10.050
You get lost or something?

416
00:25:10.050 --> 00:25:12.960
Whoa whoa whoa whoa, don't you dare!

417
00:25:12.960 --> 00:25:15.000
Don't even go there!

418
00:25:19.270 --> 00:25:21.740
It's Sniper King!

419
00:25:26.780 --> 00:25:28.550
What? He's flying!

420
00:25:28.550 --> 00:25:30.000
Awesome!

421
00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.570
Where's he been all this time?

422
00:25:38.170 --> 00:25:41.410
How is he supposed to land?

423
00:25:44.780 --> 00:25:45.720
Look at that!

424
00:25:45.720 --> 00:25:46.990
The gang's all here.

425
00:25:46.990 --> 00:25:47.950
Yoyoi!

426
00:25:47.950 --> 00:25:51.590
Quite the show, indeed!

427
00:25:51.590 --> 00:25:53.060
Sniper King!

428
00:25:53.060 --> 00:25:55.600
Although they may be
our sworn adversaries.

429
00:25:55.600 --> 00:25:59.830
To have come this far
is truly quite impressive!

430
00:26:01.530 --> 00:26:04.640
This isn't funny anymore!

431
00:26:04.640 --> 00:26:06.340
Just go away!

432
00:26:26.400 --> 00:26:28.370
C'mon Robin, work with me here!

433
00:26:29.010 --> 00:26:30.440
You can say what you want.

434
00:26:31.120 --> 00:26:33.180
If you wanna die or
whatever, that's fine,

435
00:26:33.180 --> 00:26:37.010
but when you say it,
you say it as part of our crew.

436
00:26:38.980 --> 00:26:40.450
Yeah Robin, he's right!

437
00:26:40.450 --> 00:26:42.850
Come back, Robin!

438
00:27:04.010 --> 00:27:06.110
Hey Sniper King, can you stand?

439
00:27:06.110 --> 00:27:09.080
Hm? Uh yeah, of course.

440
00:27:09.550 --> 00:27:11.800
A fall like that won't stop me!

441
00:27:17.650 --> 00:27:20.580
Really, I'll be fine.

442
00:28:05.790 --> 00:28:08.390
From now on, leave everything to us!
